   "notes": "Bene't St front of 16 Bene't St (Zizzi, in the range west of the former Barclays corner; x from the Peas Hill/Barclays end westward to 15 Bene't St). Gault/buff brick with stone dressings, tall banking-hall ground floor: from the east a large window with pediment, the entrance with a pediment and carved cartouche, then 4 windows with alternating segmental and triangular pediments (the westmost smaller). One upper floor of 6/6 sashes in stone architraves (one per bay; count read from oblique views, +-1), modillion cornice and stone balustrade (Commons photo of 16 Bene't St shows the cornice/balustrade continuing over this range). walls.json eave 4.8 m is too low (DSM); facade ~9.5 m. Positions +-0.7 m from oblique Mapillary 746178059386493 / 128550462642406 (2016)."
